 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? That's a common problem. One way to fix it is to draw thin lines under each eye, and then darken them as needed. Starting with thin lines gives you much more control. Yes, use a short curve for the nostril, and don't try to show the muscle that opens it. It' enough to show a small hole. If you draw long straight lines, you'll look like a beginner. Enjoy the practice, and don't beat yourself up if they don't look like someone you recognize. Everyone starts somewhere.",
